    "https://www.hkcend.org/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | HKCeND Careers Skip to content Hong Kong Center for Neurodegenerative Diseases HKCeND Menu About Us Open menu Vision & Mission Team Collaboration Careers Contact Us Science Open menu Platform Publication News Open menu Center News R&D and Commercialization Language Open menu English 繁體中文 简体中文 Careers Join Us When you join HKCeND, you join more than just a company, you join a dedicated team with a clear mission. Latest Oldest All Administrative Team Research Team Search Administrative Team 22 May 2026 PR and Marketing Officer (ND0070) We are seeking an experienced PR and Marketing Officer to provide hands-on support across PR, branding, and marketing initiatives.\nDuties\n\n\n \tDevelop high-quality content and materials for diverse audiences and channels, including press releases, website content, social media content, presentation decks, promotional materials, posters, brochures, and e-newsletters\n \tSupport the planning and execution of PR, branding, and marketing programs, such as press conferences, exhibitions, seminars, media briefings, and interviews\n \tHandle press and media relations, including media enquiries, interviews, and media activities\n \tCollaborate and communicate with a wide range of stakeholders to ensure the smooth delivery of PR, marketing, and branding programs\n \tPerform any other duties as assigned\n\nRequirements\n\n \tA bachelor’s degree or above, preferably in communications, marketing, public relations, journalism, science, or business\n \tMinimum 3 years of relevant experience in PR and/or marketing; experience in the life sciences or healthcare sector, public organizations, or universities is an advantage\n \tA proven track record in storytelling, writing, and editing in both English and Chinese\n \tSmart, mature, organized with pleasant personality and strong interpersonal skills\n \tAttentive to details, creative, independent, proactive, eager to learn, and able to deliver high-quality work, and flexible to meet tight schedules\n \tPossess excellent communication skills, media relations experience and network\n \tProficient in the design and production of marketing and publicity materials; basic knowledge of graphic design and photo/video production\n \tProficient in MS Office (especially PowerPoint) and Adobe Creative Cloud (Photoshop and Illustrator)\n \tGood command of spoken & written English and Chinese\n\nSalary and Benefits\nA highly competitive salary will be commensurate with qualification and experience in addition to medical and dental benefits as well as annual leave.\nThe appointment will be offered a two-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement and performance. A gratuity will be payable upon successful completion of contract.\nApplication Procedure\nApplicants should submit their up-to-date CV and cover letter with salary expectation and availability. We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the results of their applications. Review of applications will commence shortly and continue until the position is filled.\n\nThe information provided will be kept confidential and be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Administrative Team 28 Apr 2026 Assistant Project Manager (ND0069) Duties & Responsibility\nThe appointee will assist the Management in the administration of R&D projects. Duties include:\n\n \tAssist to ensure the research progress meeting the project plan\n \tPrepare reports for research projects\n \tCoordinating and liaise with internal and external parties on project administration activities\n \tProvide daily administrative support to related tasks\n \tPerform any other duties as assigned\n\nRequirements\n\n \tA bachelor’s degree in life science or a related field. PhD or master’s degree is an asset\n \tThe candidate should have at least 5 years’ relevant work experience\n \tRelevant working experience in clinical or hospital settings is an asset\n \tSelf-motivated, capable of working independently as well as in a team\n \tExcellent command of both spoken and written English and Chinese\n \tExperience in the administration of government / NGO / private foundation’s funded R&D projects is highly desirable\n \tKnowledge in research project administration, biological sample processing, patient recruitment or translational science is preferred\n \tCapability to meet deadlines\n \tProficiency in all MS software\n\nSalary and Benefits\nSalary will be commensurate with qualification and experience. Medical and dental benefits as well as annual leave will be provided. Appointment will be offered on a contract basis (Duration: 2 years), renewable subject to mutual agreement and performance.\nApplication Procedure\nApplicants should submit their up-to-date CV and cover letter with salary expectation and availability. We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the results of their applications. Review of applications will commence shortly and continue until the position is filled.\n\nThe information provided will be kept confidential and be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Research Team 22 Jul 2026 Research Assistant (ND0040) We are looking for highly energetic and motivated Research Assistants to join the Hong Kong Center for Neurodegenerative Diseases. In this role, you will support our cutting‑edge molecular neuroscience and/or genetics‑based research programs, contributing to impactful projects aimed at advancing the understanding of neurodegenerative disorders.\nDuties\n\n \tHandling and managing clinical specimens in accordance with established protocols\n \tConducting molecular biology experiments\n \tPerforming cell culture techniques\n \tExecuting cell‑based assays\n \tMaintaining and updating laboratory inventory\n \tPerforming other duties as assigned\n\nRequirements\n\n \tBachelor’s degree in Biological Sciences or a related discipline\n \tPrior experience in clinical or hospital settingsis preferred\n \tExperience in cell biology, molecular biology, genetics will be considered an advantage\n \tProficiency in Microsoft Excel is essential\n \tSelf‑motivated, detail‑oriented, and capable of working independently\n \tStrong organizational, communication, and record‑keeping skills\n\nApplication Procedure\nApplicants should submit their up-to-date CV and cover letter with salary expectation and availability. We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the results of their applications. Review of applications will commence shortly and continue until the position is filled.\n\nThe information provided will be kept confidential and be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Research Team 8 May 2026 Part-time Contract Doctor (ND0025) Duties\nMainly deployed on clinical and non-clinical duties in the following areas:\n\n \tProviding medical consultation, physical examination to study subjects in research programme related to aging and memory loss;\n \tSuccessful candidates will work in the mornings on weekdays (and potentially weekends); need to work at Hong Kong Science Park and geriatric centers around Hong Kong.\n\nRequirements\n\n \tA medical qualification registrable in Hong Kong under the Medical Registration Ordinance, Cap. 161;\n \tA good command of spoken and written Chinese and English; and\n \tBe able to speak fluent Cantonese.\n\nSalary and Benefits\nHK$800 - HK$1000 per hour depending on relevant experience. The appointment will be offered a one-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement and performance.\nApplication Procedure\nApplicants should submit their up-to-date CV and cover letter with salary expectation and availability. We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the results of their applications. Review of applications will commence shortly and continue until the position is filled.\n\nThe information provided will be kept confidential and be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Research Team 3 Feb 2026 Research Assistant (Cell Biology) (ND0029) We are seeking for highly energetic and motivated Research Assistants to join our Cell Biology team at Hong Kong Center for Neurodegenerative Diseases, based at the Hong Kong Science Park. The ideal candidate(s) will have the opportunity to actively participate and contribute to the research and development of novel strategies for high-throughput imaging-based drug discovery. Training will be provided as needed in laboratory techniques such as in vitro cell culture, performing cell treatments, immunostaining, and microscopy imaging using cutting-edge technologies.\nDuties\n\n \tSmall- and large-scale tissue culture.\n \tPerform various cell treatments such as stimulation with growth factors/cytokines, siRNA-mediated gene silencing, gene overexpression studies, etc.\n \tPerform phenotyping assays such as western blot, RT-qPCR, etc.\n \tImplement and optimize protocols for immunostaining with multiple antibodies.\n \tConfocal and live cell imaging microscopy.\n \tMaintain complete and accurate records, laboratory documentation and electronic files.\n \tPresent and discuss project progress at regular team meetings.\n \tCollaborate with other multidisciplinary teams to achieve common goals.\n \tLaboratory maintenance, i.e. ordering laboratory supplies, performing general upkeep, etc.\n \tPreparation of technical reports, summaries and quantitative analysis of data.\n\nRequirements\n\n \tBachelor’s degree in Biology/ Molecular Biology/ Biochemistry/ Biomedical Sciences or related field.\n \tWilling to work hours during weekdays and weekends depending on experimental needs.\n \tStrong interpersonal and organizational skills and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced dynamic environment.\n \tSelf-motivated, detail-oriented, team-oriented with the ability to work independently.\n \tAbility to follow oral and written instructions and to perform tasks with minimal supervision.\n \tExperience in cell biology- and molecular biology-based laboratory techniques is preferred.\n\nSalary and Benefits\nA highly competitive salary will be commensurate with qualification and experience in addition to medical and dental benefits as well as annual leave. The appointment will be offered a renewable one-year contract, subject to mutual agreement and performance.\nApplication Procedure\nApplicants should submit their up-to-date CV and cover letter with salary expectation and availability. We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the results of their applications. Review of applications will commence shortly and continue until the position is filled.\n\nThe information provided will be kept confidential and be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Research Team 20 May 2025 Research Assistant (ND0004) Duties and Responsibilities\nThe appointee will participate in a molecular neuroscience-related and/or genetic-based research programs.\nRequirements\nApplicants should have a bachelor’s degree in biological sciences or a related field. Prior experience in clinical or hospital settings is preferred. Experience and knowledge in research project administration, biological sample processing, patient recruitment or translational science is an asset. Proficiency in Microsoft Excel is essential. Self-motivation and detail-oriented with an ability to work independently is essential.\nSalary and Benefits\nA highly competitive salary will be commensurate with qualification and experience in addition to medical and dental benefits as well as annual leave. The appointment will be offered a one-year contract, renewable subject to mutual agreement and performance.\nApplication Procedure\nApplicants should submit their up-to-date CV and cover letter with salary expectation and availability. We thank applicants for their interest but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the results of their applications. Review of applications will commence shortly and continue until the position is filled.\n\nThe information provided will be kept confidential and be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Research Team 26 Feb 2025 Post-doctoral Fellows / Research Associates (ND0002) Duties\nSuccessful candidates will study the roles and the effect of genetic risk factors in neurodegenerative diseases through a systems approach, involving epigenetic, transcriptomic, and proteomics analysis. They will also be required to process and analyze human tissues, including frozen brain tissues and paraffin blocks. The positions provide exchange opportunities and the successful candidates will work closely with renowned laboratories at international institutions.\nRequirements\nApplicants should have a PhD degree in life science; background in neuroscience, neuroanatomy or a related field; and research experience in human tissues, histology and immunohistology. Knowledge of neuro-pathology, genomic DNA, RNA, and biochemistry techniques is preferred. The appointee should possess outstanding communication skills and strong passion and commitment to science, and enjoy working in a multidisciplinary and diverse team.\nSalary and Benefits\nSalary will be commensurate with qualification and experience. Medical and dental benefits as well as annual leave will be provided. Appointment will be offered on a contract basis, renewable subject to mutual agreement and performance.\nApplication Procedure\nApplicants should submit their up-to-date CV and cover letter with salary expectation and availability. We thank applicants for their interest, but advise that only shortlisted candidates will be notified of the results of their applications. Review of applications will commence shortly and continue until the position is filled.\n\nThe information provided will be kept confidential and be used for recruitment and other employment-related purposes. We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from all qualified candidates. No results found We couldn't find any matches for your search. Please try another search. HKCeND is established under the Health@InnoHK cluster, focusing on healthcare-related technologies, including molecular diagnostics, bioinformatics, drug discovery and personalized medicine. Linkedin Instagram Facebook Twitter Youtube ABOUT US Vision & Mission Team Collaboration Careers Contact Us SCIENCE Platform Publication RESOURCES News & Events LEGAL Terms of Use Privacy Policy Funding Organizations Copyright© 2026 Hong Kong Center for Neurodegenerative Diseases. All Rights Reserved. We use cookies to offer you a better browsing experience, analyze site traffic, personalize content, and serve targeted advertisements. Read about how we use cookies and how you can control them by clicking Cookie Settings. If you continue to use this site, you consent to our use of Cookies. More Info Accept Close"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192663": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Operations Management",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Tenure-track Faculty Positions in Operations Management Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: School of Business and Management: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management: Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics and Operations Management - OM group Location Hong Kong Open Date Sep 01, 2026 Deadline Oct 16, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description T en ure-track Faculty Positions in Operations Management The Department of Information Systems, Business Statistics, and Operations Management (ISOM) at the School of Business and Management, The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST), is seeking applicants for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level in Operations Management, expected to begin in July 2027. The Operations Management group within the department offers undergraduate, MSc, and PhD programs, as well as courses for the school’s MBA, EMBA, DBA, and Executive Education programs. The group plays a major role in the HKUST Li & Fung Supply Chain Institute. The department's website is http://www.bm.ust.hk/~isom . Qualifications Candidates should hold a PhD degree (or be near completion) in Operations Management or closely related disciplines and have a strong record (or demonstrate strong competence for the Assistant Professor rank) in both research and teaching. Application Instructions Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), teaching evaluations (if any), and two selected research papers, and arrange for three reference letters to be submitted by the writers. All materials should be submitted via Interfolio by October 16, 2026. For candidates presenting at the INFORMS 2026 conference, please also provide the titles, times, and venues of the presentations. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to bloc