    "https://apply.interfolio.com/190076": {
      "title": "Faculty Position(s) in Biodiversity, Ecosystem Services, and Nature-based Solutions",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Faculty Position(s) in Biodiversity, Ecosystem Services, and Nature-based Solutions Hong Kong University of Science and Technology: Academy of Interdisciplinary Studies: Division of Environment and Sustainability Location Hong Kong Open Date Jul 24, 2026 Description The Division of Environment and Sustainability at The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology is seeking applicants for substantiation-track faculty positions at all ranks (Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Professor) in the field of Biodiversity, Ecosystem Services, and Nature-based Solutions . We invite candidates whose scholarly interests intersect with multiple areas of sustainability and sustainable development. The successful candidates will play a crucial role in advancing the University’s sustainability education strategy by providing leadership, energy, and vision to a well-balanced and multi-disciplinary approach to understanding key concepts, principles, theories, and practices related to biodiversity and ecosystem services. Candidates are expected to develop or contribute to an internationally recognized research program that emphasizes collaborative research aimed at addressing complex global challenges, including biodiversity loss, ecosystem degradation, climate change impacts, and the sustainable management of natural resources/nature-based solutions. Candidates should have a strong understanding of experiential “hands-on” learning as a means of instruction for students, and an exemplary teaching record.  Successful applicants will be expected to participate in or lead collaborative interdisciplinary research teams focused on biodiversity conservation, ecosystem services assessment, and the integration of ecological models into decision-making processes under the Division’s three research themes: Air and Health Climate Adaptation and Resilience (CARE) Sustainable Finance and Net Zero Solutions The Division of Environment and Sustainability is an interdisciplinary academic unit dedicated to the use and management of natural resources in an economically efficient, environmentally compatible, and socially responsible manner.  Our faculty members publish broadly in both disciplinary journals and diverse, environmentally focused outlets, and are rewarded for working on interdisciplinary teams in applied contexts.  Depending on the candidate’s areas of expertise, a joint appointment between the Division of Environment and Sustainability and a relevant academic Department/Division may be possible. Qualifications A doctoral degree in ecology, environmental science, biology, or a related interdisciplinary field with a focus on biodiversity, ecosystem services or nature-based solutions. Proven teaching and advising experience at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. A strong research and publication record consistent with the candidate’s academic rank, along with evidence of potential for securing research funding. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in interdisciplinary teams, engaging both social and natural scientists. Application Instructions Interested candidates should complete the online application via Interfolio by clicking the \"Apply Now\" button on this page.  Please include the following application materials through Interfolio: A cover letter summarizing qualifications, areas of expertise, and career goals Full curriculum vitae Research Statement Teaching Statement Contact Information for three qualified referees Review of applications will start in early August 2026 and applications will be accepted until the positions are filled. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement HKUST is an equal opportunities employer and is committed to our core values of inclusiveness, diversity, and respect. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They m